/**
 * Sprint 11R — Golden Intent Evaluation Set: fixture corpus.
 *
 * Realistic PMFreak PM phrasing (mostly informal Spanish, as a real PM would type it) used to
 * measure real-world compatibility between the production classifier
 * (`classifier/intentClassifier.ts`) and the enriched classifier (`@/lib/conversational-brain`)
 * via the Sprint 10R adapter (`classifier/intentCompatibilityAdapter.ts`).
 *
 * `expectedProductionIntent`, `expectedEnrichedFamily`, and `expectedMappedIntent` are not guesses
 * — they were captured by actually running both classifiers (and the adapter) against `input` at
 * authoring time. That makes this corpus a regression baseline: if a future change to either
 * classifier or the adapter's mapping table changes these outputs, `runGoldenIntentEvaluation()`
 * reports a drift warning (see `intentGoldenEvaluation.ts`) rather than silently going stale.
 *
 * `shouldBeCompatible` is `expectedProductionIntent === expectedMappedIntent`, recorded explicitly.
 * Cases with a `notes` field document a real, non-obvious vocabulary gap or overlap between the
 * two classifiers' pattern lists — not a corpus mistake.
 *
 * See docs/conversational-brain-golden-intent-evaluation.md and the Sprint 11R section of
 * docs/conversational-brain-pipeline-reconciliation.md for how to run and interpret this corpus.
 */

